{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on question cf955132 (H3-mac cbcadd7f: witness (b) and the celld\npin).\n\nWitness (b) is the same-node preserve shutdown, not a peer handoff. A\npeer handoff needs a second celld process and belongs to H4. Accepted\ncompletion for one node: celld's own log shows its preserve path ran to\nits end (the sealed line, or the pinned version's equivalent signal),\nthe node record is no longer `draining`, and after the restart the\nacknowledged journal of each room reads back entry by entry (ackcheck,\nas in REPORT.md). Exit 0 or a live store alone does not count. If the\npinned celld has no single-node preserve path, the witness records the\nstall as the known single-node limit, named for Hugh as a celld\nmatter, and still proves the `down` order (store stops only after celld\nexits) and the entry-by-entry recovery; say so in the note's open\nlimits.\n\nPin: one reviewed update of apps/room/celld/celld.version from v0.6.2\nto v0.6.3 inside the H3-mac head, with H1's smoke run again at that\npin and its result in the evidence table. The kit and the physical\nwitnesses run v0.6.3, the version the validation used.\n\nRequest cbcadd7f stands with these two clarifications; no refiling.\nDX-TR landed at 11:26 (1f573145), so H3-mac is now the item in\nprogress. Retire this question when you have read the ruling.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}